import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const verifyCode = `bash conformance/a2a-server/run-1.0.sh`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="A2A conformance claims stop at the evidence."
  description="Inspect the frozen official TCK input, audited compatibility patch, exact HTTP+JSON and JSON-RPC result, and excluded surfaces."
  section="A2A conformance"
>
  <aside
    class="docs-callout docs-callout--boundary"
    aria-labelledby="a2a-proof-boundary-title"
  >
    <h2 id="a2a-proof-boundary-title">
      Server evidence, not framework certification
    </h2>
    <p>
      This gate covers the implemented A2A <code>1.0</code> HTTP+JSON and JSON-RPC/SSE
      server boundary. It does not certify a Client, gRPC, a durable application backend,
      stable APIs, or a production StateKnot release.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="a2a-result-title">
    <h2 id="a2a-result-title">Exact result</h2>
    <div
      class="docs-table-wrap"
      tabindex="0"
      aria-label="A2A TCK exact results"
    >
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Outcome</th><th>Count</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Collected</td><td>265</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Passed</td><td>177</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Declared skipped</td><td>88</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Failed / errors / xfails</td><td>0 / 0 / 0</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The per-surface report records Agent Card <code>10/10</code>, JSON-RPC
      <code>94/101</code> with seven skips, and HTTP+JSON <code>91/96</code> with
      five skips. Other skips primarily cover unconfigured gRPC and mutually exclusive
      capability branches. Skips are not counted as passes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="a2a-input-title">
    <h2 id="a2a-input-title">Freeze every executable input</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Official TCK commit <code>263b9cfaf16a554bdfb166a7ba5b67716e946349</code
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        Archive SHA-256 <code
          >694c798e93fff30f650d44bdb3db0e1768b865a4f3ddbed64ec158db209bf5db</code
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>uv 0.11.25</code>, the committed TCK lockfile under <code
          >--frozen</code
        >, and Rust <code>1.88.0</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        No expected-failures file; an independent verifier rejects drift or a
        critical skipped case.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The verifier requires executed caching, unknown-field, streaming,
      multi-subscriber, push-authentication, extended-card, HTTP error, and
      JSON-RPC SSE cases. CI uploads the complete HTML, JSON, XML, summary, and
      server log even when the run fails.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="a2a-patch-title">
    <h2 id="a2a-patch-title">Audit the harness patch</h2>
    <p>
      The pinned TCK omits the already-defined expected error metadata for
      <code>CORE-SEND-003</code> and serializes several JSON-RPC parameters with Python
      snake-case names instead of A2A camel-case wire names. The committed patch corrects
      metadata and request serialization only; it does not weaken assertions, remove
      tests, or add expected failures. The first defect is tracked in <a
        href="https://github.com/a2aproject/a2a-tck/issues/202"
        >upstream issue #202</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="a2a-reproduce-title">
    <h2 id="a2a-reproduce-title">Reproduce the gate</h2>
    <div class="docs-code" data-code-block>
      <div class="docs-code-head">
        <span>Shell · pinned official TCK</span>
        <button
          class="copy-button affordance"
          type="button"
          data-copy-button
          data-copy-target="a2a-verify-code"
        >
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre id="a2a-verify-code" tabindex="0"><code>{verifyCode}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p>
      The TCK also prints a <code>78.8%</code> aggregate over its complete requirement
      and transport inventory, including unconfigured gRPC and non-applicable branches.
      StateKnot preserves that raw output alongside the exact test counts instead
      of presenting it as 100% certification. Read the
      <a href="/docs/a2a-server/">production service obligations</a> next.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
